{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 32,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So these three men ceased to answer Job, because he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " righteous in his own eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then was kindled the wrath of Elihu the son of Barachel the Buzite, of the kindred of Ram: against Job was his wrath kindled, because he justified himself rather than God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also against his three friends was his wrath kindled, because they had found no answer, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " had condemned Job.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now Elihu had waited till Job had spoken because they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " older than he.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Elihu saw that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no answer in the mouth of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "these",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " three men, then his wrath was kindled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Elihu the son of Barachel the Buzite answered and said, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " young, and ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " very old; wherefore I was afraid, and durst not show you my opinion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I said, Days should speak, and multitude of years should teach wisdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a spirit in man: and the inspiration of the Almighty giveth them understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Great men are not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "always",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wise: neither do the aged understand judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I said, Hearken to me; I also will show my opinion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I waited for your words; I gave ear to your reasons, whilst ye searched out what to say.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, I attended to you, and behold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none of you that convinced Job, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "or",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that answered his words:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lest ye should say, We have found out wisdom: God thrusteth him down, not man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now he hath not directed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " words against me: neither will I answer him with your speeches.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They were amazed, they answered no more: they left off speaking.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I had waited, (for they spoke not, but stood still, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " answered no more;)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I said",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", I will answer also my part, I also will show my opinion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I am full of matter, the spirit within me constraineth me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, my belly ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as wine ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hath no vent; it is ready to burst like new bottles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will speak, that I may be refreshed: I will open my lips and answer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let me not, I pray you, accept any man's person, neither let me give flattering titles to man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.32.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.32.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I know not to give flattering titles; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in so doing",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", my Maker would soon take me away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
